    "body": "Three changes in the PC/SC plugin, found while running the examples of `keyple-cpp-example` on Windows with SpringCard Puck and Identive readers, including plugging and unplugging readers during a run.\n\nOne commit per defect, each message stating the observed symptom.\n\n### Commits\n\n- `5f57bba` **handle card communication errors.** `CardChannel::transmit` and `CardTerminal::connect` only tested `SCARD_W_REMOVED_CARD` and otherwise ended on a `RuntimeException(\"Should not reach here.\")`. Both now go through a predicate covering the whole family of card errors, and the message carries the PC/SC code.\n- `a3b5223` **return the symbolic name of a PC/SC error.** `PcscPluginAdapter` dispatches on `SCARD_*` symbolic names to decide whether a reader enumeration failure is recoverable, as the Java reference does, where a `PCSCException` message *is* that name. The Windows shim returned only a hexadecimal code, so none of those tests could match: the branch that clears the initialisation latch and re-establishes the PC/SC context was unreachable, and the plugin never saw a reader again once Windows stopped the Smart Card service. Also drops a shared static buffer that raced between the monitoring threads.\n- `694905c` **export `PcscCardCommunicationProtocol` from the library.** The class carried no `KEYPLEPLUGINPCSC_API` attribute, unlike the deprecated `PcscSupportedContactlessProtocol` it replaces, so its static members were not exported and no consumer could link against them. The deprecation therefore pointed users at an API they could not use, which is why the examples were still on the old one.\n\n### Relation to the `SCARD_E_NO_SMARTCARD` test on this base\n\nThis base adds `SCARD_E_NO_SMARTCARD` alongside `SCARD_W_REMOVED_CARD` in `CardTerminal::connect`. The first commit replaces that pair with `isCardCommunicationError`, which already covers both of those codes plus `SCARD_W_RESET_CARD`, `SCARD_W_UNPOWERED_CARD`, `SCARD_W_UNRESPONSIVE_CARD`, `SCARD_E_NOT_TRANSACTED`, `SCARD_E_COMM_DATA_LOST` and the internal error Windows returns on a contactless tear-off. No coverage is lost, and the `else` branch no longer throws \"Should not reach here\".\n\n### Note on the export\n\n`CMAKE_WINDOWS_EXPORT_ALL_SYMBOLS` does not rescue the third commit: it exports functions, not data, so the static members stayed invisible. The attribute is the only fix.\n\n### Validation\n\nValidated on hardware by unplugging and replugging each reader, including the last one, which is what stops the Windows Smart Card service, and by migrating the 28 protocol call sites of `keyple-cpp-example` onto the newly linkable class.\n",
